<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>A Letter to IDT Students</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: Georgia, serif; max-width: 800px; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1.5em; color: #222; line-height: 1.7; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6em; margin-bottom: 0.2em; }
  .byline { font-size: 0.9em; color: #555; margin-bottom: 2em; }
  details { margin: 1.5em 0; border-left: 3px solid #002D62; padding-left: 1em; }
  summary { font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold; color: #002D62; cursor: pointer; padding: 0.4em 0; }
  summary:hover { color: #0045a0; }
  h3 { margin-top: 1.8em; margin-bottom: 0.3em; color: #002D62; }
  .opportunity { background: #f0f4ff; border-left: 3px solid #6699cc; padding: 0.6em 1em; margin: 0.8em 0; font-size: 0.95em; }
  .skills { font-style: italic; font-size: 0.9em; color: #444; }
  ul { margin-top: 0.4em; }
  hr { border: none; border-top: 1px solid #ccc; margin: 2em 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>A Letter to IDT Students</h1>
<p class="byline">AIX Center · SUNY Polytechnic Institute · Spring 2026</p>

<hr>

<h2>A Community of AI</h2>

<p>Underlying everything in this letter is something simpler: an invitation to think together. The questions AI raises — about knowledge, about work, about what it means to be human in a world of increasingly capable machines — are not questions any of us can answer alone. The AIX Center is a community as much as a research unit, and what makes it work is people who are genuinely curious, willing to share what they're learning, and open to being surprised.</p>

<p>That's the kind of student I'm hoping to meet. Read on.</p>

<hr>

<p>I'm writing to invite you to participate in a journey of exploring artificial intelligence as you complete your degree in Information Design &amp; Technology.</p>

<p>As some of you know, I've embraced using generative AI as a tool for teaching and learning over the past few semesters, and I'll continue to adjust my approach. As I prepare for a summer of reading, reflection, and research — and in preparation

