      <h3>Analytic Capabilities — Citation Network and Digital Library Construction</h3>
      <p>This project supports the development of an analytical framework for societal vulnerability analysis, grounded in political science and used to understand conditions that precede institutional instability. The research task is building out a citation network — starting from a key anchor paper and mapping connections forward, backward, and sideways. Part digital library construction, part intellectual cartography. Much of this work is machine-assisted and would benefit from someone with library science instincts.</p>
      <div class="opp">
        <strong>Capstone / Independent Study</strong>
        Design and implement an experiment or validation/verification test suite to assess the accuracy and reliability of knowledge generated by LLMs within this analytical framework. Methodological research with real stakes — the outputs inform how AI-assisted analysis gets used and trusted.
      </div>
      <p class="skills">Skills of value: research methods, information organization, AI-assisted literature tools, interest in epistemology and knowledge quality.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>AI Literacy Curriculum — FYS 111</h3>
      <p>We are building the AI literacy curriculum for SUNY Poly's First Year Seminar from the ground up — slides, exercises, activities, and assessments — as an open educational resource. Students who join this project help shape what thousands of first-year students will encounter as their first formal introduction to AI in higher education.</p>
      <div class="opp">
        <strong>Capstone / Independent Study</strong>
        Test and refine the five-hour intro to AI curriculum and the Google AI Essentials certificate pathway. Generate a Brightspace cartridge for institutional ingestion. Refine, validate, and document that workflow end to end. An instructional design capstone with a real deliverable and a real audience.
      </div>
      <p class="skills">Skills of value: instructional design, writing, curriculum development, interest in pedagogy and learning management systems.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>AI and the Human Future — Course and Knowledge Base Development</h3>
      <p>Science, Technology, and Society studies — STS — is a discipline that refuses to treat technology as separate from the human world that produces it. It asks who built things, under what pressures, for whose benefit, and with what consequences, drawing on history, philosophy, sociology, anthropology, and cultural theory. I am building a new course — working title "AI and the Human Future" — that asks those questions of AI. How do different intellectual and cultural traditions — Indigenous knowledge systems, postcolonial theory, feminist philosophy of science, religious ethics, critical race theory — illuminate what AI is doing in the world? I'm building this course as a learner, not an STS expert.</p>
      <div class="opp">
        <strong>Capstone / Independent Study</strong>
        Build an active, annotated bibliographic tool — probably in Zotero using tags — to serve as a dynamic literature base for the introductory class launching fall 2026. Combines information architecture, library science practice, and instructional design into a single deliverable that will be used immediately.
      </div>
      <p class="skills">Skills of value: curiosity, research, information architecture, instructional design, comfort working at the edges of your knowledge.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Legal and Ethical Issues in the Information Age</h3>
      <p>The legal and ethical landscape around AI and information technology is moving fast — data center moratoriums, state versus federal preemption battles, child safety legislation, consumer protection frameworks. This is both a course under development and an ongoing research project. One organizing thread: Maslow's hierarchy of needs as a lens on information ethics — security and privacy at the safety level, identity and belonging complicated by platforms and algorithmic curation, self-actualization running up against intellectual freedom and access.</p>
      <div class="opp">
        <strong>Capstone / Independent Study</strong>
        Develop and test a workflow using a cube/voxel approach to resource organization — mapping legal, ethical, and policy resources into a multidimensional structure that allows navigation across topics, scales, and frameworks. The goal is a navigable resource architecture for the course that can be traversed in multiple directions rather than consumed linearly.
      </div>
      <p class="skills">Skills of value: research, legal and policy analysis, information architecture, writing, comfort with fast-moving material.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Workshop Design — NYHIMA and AI Training Materials</h3>
      <p>We are designing and co-delivering a three-hour AI literacy workshop for the New York Health Information Management Association — practitioners working at the intersection of healthcare, data, and technology. Real audience, real deadline (early June), real deliverable. This project connects to the broader AIX open educational resource ecosystem — the AIX Workbench, Exploring AI Chatbots, Exploring AI Agents, and Building My AI Workbench short course series.</p>
      <div class="opp">
        <strong>Capstone / Independent Study</strong>
        Design the full NYHIMA workshop as an instructional design project — learning objectives, instructional design objects, facilitation guide, and participant materials. Students credited as co-designers and co-facilitators. Timeline is tight; this one moves fast.
      </div>
      <p class="skills">Skills of value: instructional design, facilitation, writing, interest in health informatics or professional development.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Africa Partnerships — COIL and International AI Literacy</h3>
      <p>The AIX Center maintains active academic partnerships with institutions in Nigeria and Cameroon, with work focused on AI literacy, curriculum development, and institutional capacity. This work is grounded in the COIL framework — Collaborative Online International Learning — which creates structured opportunities for cross-institutional engagement across contexts. COIL itself is a rich IDT topic: designing learning experiences that work across time zones, cultures, languages, and institutional constraints is a genuine instructional design challenge with growing relevance as AI reshapes what's possible in international collaboration.</p>
      <div class="opp">
        <strong>Capstone / Independent Study</strong>
        Design and implement a COIL experience focused on AI literacy in collaboration with a partner institution in Nigeria or Cameroon. Or develop a capstone examining COIL as an instructional design framework — its affordances, constraints, and future directions in an AI-enabled environment.
      </div>
      <p class="skills">Skills of value: research, writing, cross-cultural communication, instructional design, interest in international and collaborative learning.</p>
    </div>

  </section>

